---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---

<Page
  title="Editorial policy"
  metaTitle="Editorial Policy & How We Review Resorts | SpiceVacations"
  description="How SpiceVacations researches destinations and resorts, keeps guides up to date, separates advertising and affiliate links from editorial choices, and fixes errors."
  updated="October 5, 2026"
  lead="How we research, write, update and correct every guide on SpiceVacations.com."
>
  <p>
    SpiceVacations.com publishes independent travel guides for couples planning romantic getaways, honeymoons and beach vacations across the
    United States, Mexico and the Caribbean. This page explains the standards every page on the site has to meet.
  </p>

  <h2>How we research</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Primary sources first.</strong> Facts such as locations, adults-only policies, entry rules and park reservations are checked against official sources: the resort itself, tourism boards, the U.S. State Department and the National Park Service.</li>
    <li><strong>No invented data.</strong> We never publish made-up prices, star ratings, reviews, awards or "only 2 rooms left" claims. A rating appears only when it comes from a named, linked source.</li>
    <li><strong>Practical, couple-focused angles.</strong> Each resort profile says who the property suits, who should skip it, and what to know before booking, so you can rule places out as quickly as you rule them in.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we choose what to feature</h2>
  <p>
    We feature established destinations and resorts with a consistent reputation among couples. Commission rates and advertising never decide
    whether a property is included or how it is ranked. Some properties we recommend have no affiliate link at all.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising and affiliate links</h2>
  <p>
    The site is funded by affiliate commissions and, where shown, display advertising. Ads are labeled "Advertisement," are served by third parties
    such as Google, and are kept separate from editorial content. Advertisers have no say over what we write. Read our
    <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> and <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>Photos and illustrations</h2>
  <p>
    Photos come from free stock libraries such as Pexels and Pixabay and are credited on each page. Where a photo shows the general area rather than the exact resort, we label it
    "representative photo of the area." A small number of mood images on our home page and vacation-type pages are generated with AI. They are always labeled "AI-generated image," are used only for general scenes such as a beach at sunset, and never depict or stand in for a real resort, room or destination landmark. Our own brand illustrations are used when no suitable photo is available. See <a href="/photo-credits/">photo credits</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates and corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Every guide shows a "last updated" date. We review guides regularly, and sooner when policies, entry requirements or seasons change. If you spot
    an error, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or use our <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>. We correct factual errors
    promptly and update the date on the page.
  </p>

  <h2>Who writes our guides</h2>
  <p>
    Guides are written and edited by the SpiceVacations Editorial Team. Learn more <a href="/about/">about us</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
